(7394571, 1163023, 65858, '<td valign="top">Wow, at first glance this doesn''t look real. I''m fascinated! 8 for now.</td>', 'Wow, at first glance this doesn''t look real. I''m fascinated! 8 for now.', '2015-08-03 02:39:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394572, 1163048, 65858, '<td valign="top">Hmm, a bit too bright for a "silhouette" for me. Darn city lights. ;)</td>', 'Hmm, a bit too bright for a "silhouette" for me. Darn city lights. ;)', '2015-08-03 02:42:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394573, 1162993, 65858, '<td valign="top">Interesting, hard to tell whether it''s at night, though.</td>', 'Interesting, hard to tell whether it''s at night, though.', '2015-08-03 02:42:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394574, 1163022, 65858, '<td valign="top">Really nicely done!</td>', 'Really nicely done!', '2015-08-03 02:43:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394605, 1162958, 180777, '<td valign="top">tHIS is stunning. Beautiful. Maybe the foreground focus is not perfect? The vingetting is a bit much for my tastes. But otherwise, who am I to say anything about this, an awesome picture and my favorite so far, by far. I''m new to this DP Challenge, so I hope these comments help.</td>', 'tHIS is stunning. Beautiful. Maybe the foreground focus is not perfect? The vingetting is a bit much for my tastes. But otherwise, who am I to say anything about this, an awesome picture and my favorite so far, by far. I''m new to this DP Challenge, so I hope these comments help.', '2015-08-03 04:09:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394607, 1163023, 180777, '<td valign="top">This would be a ten in my view if the colors had more depth and the contrasts were more defined. But all I can do is "comment" because I''m just getting started myself, and this is an astonishing photograph, well planned and I could stare at it for quite a while. Thank you for sharing it</td>', 'This would be a ten in my view if the colors had more depth and the contrasts were more defined. But all I can do is "comment" because I''m just getting started myself, and this is an astonishing photograph, well planned and I could stare at it for quite a while. Thank you for sharing it', '2015-08-03 04:13:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394608, 1163004, 180777, '<td valign="top">This is conceptually and aesthetically beautiful to me. I''m just getting started on photography and this is inspiring, so thanks for sharing</td>', 'This is conceptually and aesthetically beautiful to me. I''m just getting started on photography and this is inspiring, so thanks for sharing', '2015-08-03 04:15:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394609, 1163020, 180777, '<td valign="top">I can''t choose between this and one other, this is so beautiful. I''m not qualified technically to offer feedback to you, I''ve just started recently on photography myself, but this is appealing on so many levels. The title; the composition, colors, contrasts, clarity in appropriate places, sentiment, and theme. Thank you so much for sharing it, I will study it as an example as I move forward in my own art.</td>', 'I can''t choose between this and one other, this is so beautiful. I''m not qualified technically to offer feedback to you, I''ve just started recently on photography myself, but this is appealing on so many levels. The title; the composition, colors, contrasts, clarity in appropriate places, sentiment, and theme. Thank you so much for sharing it, I will study it as an example as I move forward in my own art.', '2015-08-03 04:18:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394610, 1163045, 180777, '<td valign="top">If I find myself staring at a picture for more than a few seconds, I have to stop staring and analyze. This is beautiful! The subject matter - a lot of people take pix of themselves with their children. That isn''t unusual, and the parents/kids are usually wonderful. But what is so wonderful about this picture to me are the colors, contrasts, the flowing currents between people and nature, the balance between the layers, the framing. It''s beautiful. I think the focus is off in places, and that there might be a little more contrast between the elements in it (it seems too soft to me - maybe softness could have been conveyed only on the human subjects) - but this is awesome and thank you for sharing.</td>', 'If I find myself staring at a picture for more than a few seconds, I have to stop staring and analyze. This is beautiful! The subject matter - a lot of people take pix of themselves with their children. That isn''t unusual, and the parents/kids are usually wonderful. But what is so wonderful about this picture to me are the colors, contrasts, the flowing currents between people and nature, the balance between the layers, the framing. It''s beautiful. I think the focus is off in places, and that there might be a little more contrast between the elements in it (it seems too soft to me - maybe softness could have been conveyed only on the human subjects) - but this is awesome and thank you for sharing.', '2015-08-03 04:18:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394611, 1162801, 180777, '<td valign="top">I''m new to this (photography and DP challenge) so please take whatever I say in view of that, I''m not sure my "critique" verbiage is written in an acceptable way.<br/> <br/>I really like this photograph a lot. On a gut level it feels right because it is balanced, it has clarity that I can focus on, I think it captures "silhouettes" in an interesting way. The large, rock silhouette on the right - it''s like a profile shot of an ancient face, it seems to be glowing through the nose and it is touching the sun. It''s beautiful. The silhouette of that stonehenge looking formation in the upper-middle left - legs maybe of a giant? very nice. The lighting in the foreground is also very illuminating, I can see the barnacles on the rocks. The lines/depth are following nicely from left to right. If there were any criticism, it might be that some of the image is out of focus - but then again that adds nicely to the dream effect.</td>', 'I''m new to this (photography and DP challenge) so please take whatever I say in view of that, I''m not sure my "critique" verbiage is written in an acceptable way. I really like this photograph a lot. On a gut level it feels right because it is balanced, it has clarity that I can focus on, I think it captures "silhouettes" in an interesting way. The large, rock silhouette on the right - it''s like a profile shot of an ancient face, it seems to be glowing through the nose and it is touching the sun. It''s beautiful. The silhouette of that stonehenge looking formation in the upper-middle left - legs maybe of a giant? very nice. The lighting in the foreground is also very illuminating, I can see the barnacles on the rocks. The lines/depth are following nicely from left to right. If there were any criticism, it might be that some of the image is out of focus - but then again that adds nicely to the dream effect.', '2015-08-03 04:19:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394612, 1162962, 180777, '<td valign="top">It''s beautiful, and how you have the faces barely visible. The contrast, focus, leaves, the window panes and separation between things. There is a lot of mystery and a certain "come home please" in this. Sort of like, "you''re not here right now, so this is all we will let you see; but there''s more, just come home" - thx for sharing</td>', 'It''s beautiful, and how you have the faces barely visible. The contrast, focus, leaves, the window panes and separation between things. There is a lot of mystery and a certain "come home please" in this. Sort of like, "you''re not here right now, so this is all we will let you see; but there''s more, just come home" - thx for sharing', '2015-08-03 04:19:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394613, 1162987, 180777, '<td valign="top">I''m new to this so I hope my comments help. I love the balance in this, and the contrasts - I really like how the peakock is looking left over its'' shoulder in the direction that it is. I love the composition in other words! The focus is impressive to me - something I have trouble with. I can''t think of anything really critiqy to say about it - other than the lower right quadrant looses a bit of the vibrance that the rest of the picture has, and also, if it''s the moon in the light behind the clouds, I might have tried to capture more of the shape/color of the moon somehow (not sure how! but maybe with an exposure that had a fast shutter speed, super low ISO and an F number between 3.2 - 5.6)<br/> <br/>Thanks for sharing this pic!</td>', 'I''m new to this so I hope my comments help. I love the balance in this, and the contrasts - I really like how the peakock is looking left over its'' shoulder in the direction that it is. I love the composition in other words! The focus is impressive to me - something I have trouble with. I can''t think of anything really critiqy to say about it - other than the lower right quadrant looses a bit of the vibrance that the rest of the picture has, and also, if it''s the moon in the light behind the clouds, I might have tried to capture more of the shape/color of the moon somehow (not sure how! but maybe with an exposure that had a fast shutter speed, super low ISO and an F number between 3.2 - 5.6) Thanks for sharing this pic!', '2015-08-03 04:19:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394614, 1162635, 180777, '<td valign="top">I am new to this, so forgive please! I would rate this 5.5 - 5.9. It would be a 6.5 or 7 but for the missed opportunity to capture the full extent of the moon. The birds, limbs, focus, composition, color and contrast are all really beautiful in this. But the moon could have (IMH)) been caught in a second layer, with lower ISO, faster shutter speed and an F number between 3.2 and 5.6. I might have also increased the contrast a bit because there is also some missed opportunity in too much uniformity (again only my opinion!) in the blue''s and that could have really been exploited. <br/>Otherwise, I really like this picture a lot, and thanks for sharing.</td>', 'I am new to this, so forgive please! I would rate this 5.5 - 5.9. It would be a 6.5 or 7 but for the missed opportunity to capture the full extent of the moon. The birds, limbs, focus, composition, color and contrast are all really beautiful in this. But the moon could have (IMH)) been caught in a second layer, with lower ISO, faster shutter speed and an F number between 3.2 and 5.6. I might have also increased the contrast a bit because there is also some missed opportunity in too much uniformity (again only my opinion!) in the blue''s and that could have really been exploited. Otherwise, I really like this picture a lot, and thanks for sharing.', '2015-08-03 04:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394616, 1162939, 180777, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot. It presents well conceptually. The only critique I would have is that it is a little out of focus - a nice effect if that''s what you meant. Also, that the moon is a bit bright - how cool to have layered maybe? and have the moon be shot with faster shutter, lower ISO and a super fast shutter, while in focus, with the foreground being either blurry, or clear? I dunno, I''m new to photography challenges on DP (new as a photographer) so don''t know exactly what to write. The light, on the hand facing the moon, in this photo is beautiful - especially if sharper? thank you for sharing!</td>', 'I like this a lot. It presents well conceptually. The only critique I would have is that it is a little out of focus - a nice effect if that''s what you meant. Also, that the moon is a bit bright - how cool to have layered maybe? and have the moon be shot with faster shutter, lower ISO and a super fast shutter, while in focus, with the foreground being either blurry, or clear? I dunno, I''m new to photography challenges on DP (new as a photographer) so don''t know exactly what to write. The light, on the hand facing the moon, in this photo is beautiful - especially if sharper? thank you for sharing!', '2015-08-03 04:20:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394617, 1162993, 180777, '<td valign="top">i like this a lot. the symettry between leaves and cloud formations. the contrasts in the land below the leaves are welcoming, like puzzle pieces. It feels a little over exposed? i like the things you have going on in the lower right corner, they look like people or things marching onwards past the frame but can''t quite make out what they are! I also like the use of negative (in this case positive?) white/negative space :) I think that the compositional selection of sparse elements is outstanding.</td>', 'i like this a lot. the symettry between leaves and cloud formations. the contrasts in the land below the leaves are welcoming, like puzzle pieces. It feels a little over exposed? i like the things you have going on in the lower right corner, they look like people or things marching onwards past the frame but can''t quite make out what they are! I also like the use of negative (in this case positive?) white/negative space :) I think that the compositional selection of sparse elements is outstanding.', '2015-08-03 04:20:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394618, 1163035, 180777, '<td valign="top">I like the synergy between the movements of the dancers, and the movement in the statues. Nice job of capturing that. The colors are also really nice, and textures. Somehow you captured color and silhouettes in a shot - my critiques would be that the focus could be sharper on the silhouettes (or they could be super blurry with more focus on the other elements) but the focus doesn''t change much between them; and also maybe the silhouettes and foreground could have been sharper, and darker or with more contrast. I just love the overall composition though, and it''s cool being able to see the people in the background subtlety behind the statues. I would give this a "5.5 - 5.8" but they only allow for 5 or 6</td>', 'I like the synergy between the movements of the dancers, and the movement in the statues. Nice job of capturing that. The colors are also really nice, and textures. Somehow you captured color and silhouettes in a shot - my critiques would be that the focus could be sharper on the silhouettes (or they could be super blurry with more focus on the other elements) but the focus doesn''t change much between them; and also maybe the silhouettes and foreground could have been sharper, and darker or with more contrast. I just love the overall composition though, and it''s cool being able to see the people in the background subtlety behind the statues. I would give this a "5.5 - 5.8" but they only allow for 5 or 6', '2015-08-03 04:20:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394619, 1162996, 180777, '<td valign="top">I like the color and richness in this. The intimidating presence of the bull, and the title, I think it is titled well. The colors are balanced IMHO and the terrain, the angles. I can''t tell on the focus though - I think it''s good, but the richness and darkness in the colors actually loose some of the focus that I can see. If I were editing this awesome image I would not do much to it at all except draw out more contrast to allow enough space for both light and dark spectrums, because right now (to me) the potential of this story seems constrained behind darkness. I think it is a beautiful picture though</td>', 'I like the color and richness in this. The intimidating presence of the bull, and the title, I think it is titled well. The colors are balanced IMHO and the terrain, the angles. I can''t tell on the focus though - I think it''s good, but the richness and darkness in the colors actually loose some of the focus that I can see. If I were editing this awesome image I would not do much to it at all except draw out more contrast to allow enough space for both light and dark spectrums, because right now (to me) the potential of this story seems constrained behind darkness. I think it is a beautiful picture though', '2015-08-03 04:21:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394620, 1163034, 180777, '<td valign="top">I can see the kitty, and the depth of field; the command over lighting, the correct ISO (low) and low exposure speed for at night. I really like this picture. If you could bring out some of the very, very foreground and sharpen up the cat''s outline - including its'' eyes, that would be wow. Thx for sharing!</td>', 'I can see the kitty, and the depth of field; the command over lighting, the correct ISO (low) and low exposure speed for at night. I really like this picture. If you could bring out some of the very, very foreground and sharpen up the cat''s outline - including its'' eyes, that would be wow. Thx for sharing!', '2015-08-03 04:21:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394650, 1162987, 179769, '<td valign="top">To my eye, this would benefit hugely from a tighter crop.  Lovely, though!</td>', 'To my eye, this would benefit hugely from a tighter crop.  Lovely, though!', '2015-08-03 09:48:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7394653, 1163042, 179769, '<td valign="top">This would have scored higher had it been in focus.</td>', 'This would have scored higher had it been in focus.', '2015-08-03 10:04:56.000000', NULL, 1),
